🧠 Login Greeter Script

A personal Bash project built in my home lab environment.
When I log into my Ubuntu VM, this script greets me by name, shows the date and time, local Kansas City weather, top KC headlines, a random dad joke, and a motivational quote to start the day.

⚙️ Features

📅 Displays current day, date, and time

🌤 Fetches live Kansas City weather data

📰 Pulls top 5 local news headlines (with clickable links)

🤣 Generates a random “dad joke”

💬 Prints a motivational quote of the day

🧩 Modular Bash functions (easy to expand)

🧠 Runs automatically at login (optional)

🚀 How to Run
chmod +x login_greeter.sh
./login_greeter.sh


If you want it to run automatically each time you open a terminal, add this line to the bottom of your ~/.bashrc file:

~/michaelcieslewski2-TruckstoTech.github.io/projects/greeting-script/login_greeter.sh

🧰 Requirements

Bash (tested on Ubuntu 22.04+)

Python 3 (preinstalled on Ubuntu)

curl command-line tool

Internet connection (for weather and news APIs)

🧩 Code Overview
Function	Description
greet()	Displays the welcome message and timestamp
weather()	Fetches current weather for Kansas City
local_news()	Grabs live KC headlines via Google News & KCUR RSS feeds
dad_joke()	Prints a random dad joke
quote_of_the_day()	Shows a motivational quote
say()	Formats text output for color and style
🧪 Future Improvements

Add color-coded weather icons (🌧, 🌞, ❄️)

Add random tech tip of the day

Cache last news feed for offline mode

Add configuration file (~/.greeter.conf) for user city and preferences

